  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Critical fix for LC045 (Missing Include): reading a navigation through a chained null-conditional — order?.Customer?.Name — sent the analyzer into infinite recursion, and the resulting StackOverflowException is uncatchable, so it crashed the csc process itself and failed the whole build (reported from a production codebase on 5.6.0). Conditional-access placeholders now resolve to their owning access, the mixed shape order?.Customer.Address?.City is fixed too, and the null-guarded collection mutation order?.Items?.Add(x) no longer produces a false positive now that the shape analyzes instead of crashing. If you disabled the rule with dotnet_diagnostic.LC045.severity = none, it is safe to re-enable on 5.6.1.",
